# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> (lattice system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> "lattice system"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> "lattice type"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> "lattice system is a quality of crystal lattice that defines its symmetry based on the 7 categories originating from its point group symmetries of their empty translational frameworks"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>) ObjectAllValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>)))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000390> ObjectExactCardinality(1 ObjectInverseOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001927>) <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392> (lattice system value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392> "lattice system value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392> "lattice system value is a categorical value specification which describes the grouping of
lattice system based on the point group symmetries of their empty translational frameworks. The specific values are triclinic, monoclinic, orthorhombic, tetragonal, rhombohedral, hexagonal, and cubic."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000033> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000392> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> (lattice point)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> "Add axioms to PMDco (owl:tOP --> location of /located in)
1. 'solid solution' and ('has member' some 
('pure substance' and ('has part' some 
(entity and (owl:topObjectProperty some 'lattice point'))) and ('has role' some 'solute role')))
2. owl:topObjectProperty some 'lattice point'")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> "lattice point"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> "A lattice point is a fiat point that represents a position in a crystal lattice at which structural entities are regularly arranged."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> (atom site)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> "If the atom site and the lattice point have the same coordinates, i.e., the basis vector is (0, 0, 0), one can say that lattice point is located in atom site. 

The nessesity of this class came from the description of different metallic phases, as most of them are characterized by atoms occupying certain atom sites which not always coinside with lattice points.

Additionally, asserting triple \"atom located in lattice point\" contradicts the RO's definition of \"located in\" which states that r1 is located in r2 iff r1 is fully inside r2 (Kamilla's free interpretation), but here we want to merely express that an atom occupies certain position in a lattice (incl. voids). But the word \"occupies\" is used in BFO to express the relation between spatial region and any other independent continuant."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> "TODO: add a class to GDCs to replace value specification with \"fractional coordinate\" or coordinate specification or smth."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> "atom site"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> "Atom site is a site that is part of crystal lattice whose position is determined by an offset of a basis vector from a lattice point, and that is the location of a single atom"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> "Octahedral interstitial site in bcc has a reference lattice point with (1/2, 1/2, 0) basis vector"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000029>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000440> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000405>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000441> (basis vector)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000441> "basis vector"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000441> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> (regular atom site)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> "regular atom site"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000441>)))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000441>))
DisjointClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000442> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443> (intersitital site)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443> "intersitital site"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443> "void")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443> "interstitial site is a site that is located between regular lattice points in a crystal structure."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000439>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000445> (octahedral void)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000445> "octahedral void"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000445> "octahedral void is an interstitial site in a close-packed lattice where one triangular void from the top layer of spheres (atoms or ions) sits over the triangular gap of the bottom layer."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000445> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000446> (tetrahedral void)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000446> "tetrahedral void"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000446> "tetrahedral void is an interstitial site in a close-packed lattice where one sphere (atom or ion) from the top layer sits in the triangular gap formed by 3 spheres of the bottom layer."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000446> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000443>)


############################
#   Named Individuals
############################

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> (triclinic)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> "triclinic"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> "Triclinic crystal system is a crystal system with only translational symmetry."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> (monoclinic)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> "monoclinic"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> "Monoclinic crystal system is a crystal system with one twofold rotation axis or one mirror plane."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> (orthorhombic)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> "orthorhombic"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> "Orthorhombic crystal system is a crystal system with three twofold rotation axes or one twofold rotation axis and two mirror planes"@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> (tetragonal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> "tetragonal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> "Tetragonal crystal system is a crystal system with one fourfold rotation axis."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000033> (rhombohedral)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000033> "rhombohedral"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000033> "Rhombohedral crystal system is a crystal system with one threefold rotation axis."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> (hexagonal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> "hexagonal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> "Hexagonal crystal system is a crystal system with one sixfold rotation axis."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035> (cubic)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035> "cubic"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035> "Cubic crystal system is a crystal system with fourfold rotation axes."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> (primitive)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> "primitive"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> "P")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> "Primitive centering type is a centering type, where lattice points are located only on the corners of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (0,0,0)."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> (body centered)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> "body centered"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> "I")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> "Body centered centering type is a centering type, where lattice points are located  on the corners of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (0,0,0), and at the center of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (1/2,1/2,1/2)."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> (face centered)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> "face centered"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> "F")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> "Face centered centering type is a centering type, where lattice points are located  on the corners of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (0,0,0), and at the center of each faces of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (1/2,1/2,0), (1/2,0,1/2), and (0,1/2,1/2)."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046> (base centered)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046> "Add symbol annotation property")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046> "base centered"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046> "C")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046> "Base centered centering type is a centering type, where lattice points are located on the corners of a unit cell, i.e., at coordinates (0,0,0), and one additional lattice point is located at the center of a base of the cell, i.e., at coordinates (1/2,1/2,0)."@en)

# Individual: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000391> (trigonal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000391> "trigonal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000391> "Triclinic crystal system is a crystal system with one 3-fold rotation axis"@en)


)